{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1465989-character-build-test-talent","id":1465989,"title":"Character Build Test: Talent","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-31T02:04:33-07:00","id":1465989,"title":"Character Build Test: Talent","content":"Alright let's test this out and see if I got it down. Please give feedback if I got something wrong.<br /> <br /> Alright, first let's start with concept. I'm thinking &quot;Everyman Investigator into the Odd.&quot; Basically no combat skills and no world class skills, though he has received training after being Inspired so he is now fairly skilled in a variety of disciplines. He grew up poor and distracted himself with hidden tales of the fantastic that he discovered through private research. One day after surviving an accident he realized he really should be dead, but someone or something fudged the dice in his favor. This insight opened a whole new world for him and he soon found himself with an invitation to join the Aeon Society.<br /> <br /> Now Aspirations. For short term one will be experience or cause a dramatic edit. The other will be to discover something strange. For a long term Aspiration my character would like to discover one of the Aeon Societies secrets.<br /> <br /> Okay, now Step Two: Paths. I think I'll try my hand at making my own Paths. At least for Origin and Role.<br /> <br /> For Origin I'll use Street Rat as a base but switch out some stuff that doesn't make sense. I think I'll call the Path &quot;Street Rat Escapist&quot;. My character grew up on the streets but kept his nose clean, Still, the harsh nature of such a life encouraged him to find escape in books and movies. At times he also needed to literally escape bad situations, which meant being quick and strong willed. Path skills are Athletics, Enigmas, Culture and Survival. I dropped Larceny for Culture, my character didn't join a gang but spent his time in libraries and movie theaters. Edges are Adrenaline Spike, Always Prepared, Danger Sense, Hair Trigger Reflexes, Iron Will, Hardy, Mr. Fix-It, Speed Reading, Swift. Dropped Alternate Identity and Tough Cookie for Iron Will, Speed Reading and Swift.<br /> <br /> Okay for Role I think I'll go with a variation on Detective. My character is a &quot;Streetwise Archivist&quot;. He spends his time, whether it be for organizations he works for or on his own free time, collecting information and making it available for others. He is not afraid to go into the field to get information. Skills are Enigmas, Humanities, Integrity and Persuasion. Switched out Aim for Humanities. Edges are Fame, Free Running, Library, Photographic Memory, Swift and Tough Cookie. Dropped Alternate Identity and Fast Draw for Fame and modified Any One Style Edge to be limited to Free Running.<br /> <br /> For Society I'll just go with vanilla Aeon Society. My character finds that the Society's focus on understanding the world resonates with him, though he is a bit more neutral on the stated mission of uplifting and guiding humanity.<br /> <br /> For his Origin of &quot;Street Rat Escapist&quot; my character will take 1 dot in Athletics, Enigmas and Culture. For Connections his community will be local libraries and his contact will be someone he grew up with and who now has a job as a librarian at a prestigious public library. For Edges he'll take Speed Reading and Swift.<br /> <br /> For his Role of &quot;Streetwise Archivist&quot; my character will take 1 dot in Enigmas and 2 dots in Humanities. For Connections his community will be his former clients who paid him to preserve and expand their private collections of esoteric information. His contact will be a popular host of a web broadcast devoted to strange happenings and secret history. For his Edge he'll take the 2 dot version of Photographic Memory with the intention of increasing it later.<br /> <br /> For his Allegiance of &quot;Aeon Society&quot; my character will take 1 dot in Enigmas and 2 dots in Pilot. For Connections his community will be the various archivists that record the Aeon Societies discoveries and his contact will be his recruiter who was also the person indirectly responsible for him becoming a Talent. For his Edge he'll take the 2 dot version of Library with the intention of increasing it later.<br /> <br /> Now we're on Step Three. Of my six additional dots I'll spend 2 in Culture, 1 in Humanities and 3 in Science. In the end my character has Athletics at 1 dot, Culture at 3 dots (Specialty in Film), Enigma at 3 dots (Specialty in Paranormal Phenomena, Skill Trick in Connecting The Dots), Humanities at 3 dots (Specialty in History) and 2 dots in Pilot.<br /> <br /> Step four: Attributes. I'm thinking Mental, Physical then Social. My character is a man of thought but can get his hands dirty. Not so good with people, though. His favored approach is Resilience. His Intellect is 3, Cunning 3 and Resolve is 4 with his favored approach. His Might is 2, Dexterity is 3 and his Stamina is 3 with his favored approach. His Presence is 2, Manipulation is 1 and Composure is 3 with his favored approach.<br /> <br /> Step Five: Apply Talent Template<br /> <br /> My character's moment of Inspiration was the realization that someone else had used Dramatic Editing to save his life. This insight gave him an additional dot in Cunning, raising it to 4.<br /> <br /> The character has a dot in the Intuitive, Reflective and Destructive Facets of Inspiration, giving him an Inspiration rating of 4.<br /> <br /> His Gifts are Behold the Halo, That's Bad Luck, Fortean Experience and Mystery Archeology.<br /> <br /> Step Six: Final Touches.<br /> <br /> For my characters bonus attribute I'll raise Manipulation by 1 for a new total of 2. For the 4 extra points in Edges I get first I'll raise Library by 1 to a new total of 3. My character has a large collection of books and other written material that he has confirmed has not been altered in any fashion that goes into deep detail on the worlds secret history. Then I'll raise my characters Photographic Memory to 3. Then I'll buy wealth 2 to represent the nice paycheck my character gets by working for the Aeon Society.<br /> <br /> My characters health is Maimed, Injured, Injured and Bruised.<br /> <br /> My Characters Defense is 1.<br /> <br /> So is that look about right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}